ges, laid singly on tendrils, stipules and old leaves. Mature larva (Fig. 42 g-h) - body white with black irregular rings on dorsum and sides; base of each scoli with red spots fused together forming small red bands (in P. dido with orange spots). Scoli large and black (in P. dido orange with black tips); head capsule bright red with head scoli black. Prolegs on abdominal segments red (yellow in P. dido). Pupa - mottled brown and gray covered with warts; abdomen and thorax have keels; generally resembles a bird dropping.","","text","",""]]},"L7YNQ":{"d":[["Sweden","SE","iso","",""]]},"LD29":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"LJ975":{"d":[["Denmark","DK","iso","","not evaluated"]]},"M2SFC":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"MBQYB":{"d":[["Distribution. Brazil (Bahia [new record], Espirito Santo, Minas Gerais, Rio de Janeiro, Sao Paulo)","","text","",""]]},"MDDN8":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"N6GP":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"NPRK":{"d":[["Tasmania","8891","mrgid","",""]]},"NXSNT":{"d":[["","TW","iso","native",""]]},"P3YK4":{"d":[["Distribution. Mexico (Oaxaca, San Luis Potosí, Veracruz) (Fig. 1).","","text","",""]]},"PB5FN":{"d":[["Oceania","","text","",""]]},"PGT8X":{"d":[["ISO 3166-2:CA-BC","","text","native",""]]},"PRHQ":{"d":[["South America","","text","",""]]},"Q82G9":{"d":[["Europe & Northern Asia (excluding China)","","text","",""]]},"Q98Y":{"d":[["Madagascan(Madagascar)","","text","",""]]},"Q998":{"d":[["Afrotropical(Ivory Coast, Senegal)","","text","",""]]},"QHCSL":{"d":[["Distribution. Australia: New South Wales, Northern Territory, Queensland, South Australia.","","text","",""]]},"QHD2L":{"d":[["Distribution. Australia: Northern Territory, Queensland.","","text","",""]]},"QYJQV":{"d":[["DISTRIBUTION: E. Honduras to S. Ecuador.","","text","",""]]},"RC2B2":{"d":[["Norway","NO","iso","",""],["Norway","NO","iso","",""]]},"RHVK":{"d":[["CHS-HN","CHS-HN","tdwg","",""]]},"RPFS":{"d":[["Mexico to Costa Rica","","text","",""]]